🚽 Test case: #206 (3e) -- a `yap` (char) array field specifically, to
🚽 exercise the width/signedness-correct read/write paths #243 fixed for
🚽 packed char storage in this new struct-field-array code path too, not
🚽 just the array-variable and scalar-struct-field ones. Elements are
🚽 written out of order (index 0 last), matching #243's own write-order
🚽 fixtures: if a regression ever widened this field's element writes
🚽 back to 4 bytes, index 0's write would clobber indices 1-3.
gang Name {
    yap letters[4];
};

skibidi main {
    gang Name n;
    n.letters[1] = 'i';
    n.letters[2] = 'z';
    n.letters[3] = 'z';
    n.letters[0] = 'r';
    yapping("%c%c%c%c", n.letters[0], n.letters[1], n.letters[2],
           n.letters[3]);
}
